      {
        "id": 35660,
        "name": "Christopher",
        "username": "Christopher",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/christopher/{size}/1851_2.png",
        "created_at": "2012-08-01T13:44:44.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"&quot;&quot;ketigid&quot;&quot;\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n \"\"ketigid\"\":</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Just to add, I don’t think they’re giving out any promo cards with purchase either (they used to give them out for free at conventions). This time, you have to work <em>really</em> hard to earn those promos. This means sitting down and playing and winning and having a good time. Man, that’s hard work.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Well, when you buy the game, you get Sentinels Points equal to “cost” of the promo cards you would normally get, so you can choose to immediately turn those Sentinels Points into the promos you would normally get, OR you can collect those Sentinels Points and sit and play the game to gain even more and get more/better promos!</p>\n<p>Unfortunately, we are not planning on a combined package deal, however, the amount of game/number of cards (and dividers, and tokens…) in each box is very impressive for the low price.  Seriously, where else are you going to get 578 card, especially with so little repetition, plus divider cards and tokens, for only $40?</p>",
        "post_number": 5,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:09:31.984Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "incoming_link_count": 0,
